  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.6.0 — The rate controller now consumes the network feedback it always advertised. EstimatedAvailableBitrateBps acts as a hard bitrate ceiling (loss and RTT heuristics still cut below it, so a stale estimator cannot mask congestion). Jitter is a queueing early warning that holds bitrate increases without ever triggering a cut. ClientDecodeDelay drives the speed/fps/resolution complexity cascade and never touches bitrate or QP — a client falling behind is a different problem from network congestion. FIXED: the severe-congestion RTT test used an absolute 100 ms threshold, so any link with a higher baseline RTT sat permanently in severe congestion; it is now baseline-relative, as is the recovery gate, which previously used an absolute 40 ms and could leave a high-baseline link unable to walk back up after a loss episode. Callers who supply none of these fields get decisions identical to 0.5.0, verified against a 600-frame decision transcript captured from the 0.5.0 controller. Encoding is byte-identical to 0.5.0.",
